Ticket **#4471** was marked known as a single parser bug: the shared parser reads
dates month-first while day-first tenants write the day first. The merge count is
**412** unique reports.

The live cause table disagrees. The same 412 reports resolve to **two** causes.
Only one of them is the ticket the desk kept.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one problem. Open one engineering ticket per cause below.
</Callout>

## Causes in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets to file

1. **parser** — 379 reports. Shared parser reads month first; day-first tenants
   (app, email, and booking-v2 form) get flipped dates. This is the cause #4471
   already claims.
2. **hint** — 33 reports. booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date
   field while the form still reads the tenant's day-first way. Form-only,
   three tenants (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour). Needs its own
   ticket; it is not the parser.

Intake tags disagree with cause often enough that tagging alone cannot justify
the merge. Deduping by subject (decision 0001) put both causes into one thread.

